  "text": "Subscribe to skip adsAdvertisementAstronomyA Stunning Nebula Image Predicts How Our Sun Will DieA light show lasting 25,000 yearsDNBy David Nield10:30 AM CDT on October 16, 2026Add Nautilus to GoogleFast-forward five billion years or so, and our own sun will look something like this: the Messier 27 (M27) planetary nebula, also known as the Dumbbell Nebula. It’s a vast cloud of gas and dust, ejected by a dying sun, and lit up by the star’s last embers.Powered By 10 ShareNextStayThis spectacular image of M27 was captured by astrophotographer Andrew McCarthy, over the course of 30 hours and several nights, in order to avoid both the sun and the Earth getting in the way of the shot.The M27 planetary nebula: Oxygen in blue, hydrogen and sulfur in orange. Credit: Andrew McCarthySubscribe to skip adsAdvertisement",
